#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:10
msgid "Finding problematic bits of code using grep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:12
msgid ""
"Just run `grep -nrE '[^a-zA-Z](Slow)?Buffer\\s*\\(' --exclude-dir "
"node_modules`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:14
msgid ""
"It will find all the potentially unsafe places in your own code (with "
"some considerably unlikely exceptions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:17
msgid "Finding problematic bits of code using Node.js 8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:19
msgid ""
"If you’re using Node.js ≥ 8.0.0 (which is recommended), Node.js exposes "
"multiple options that help with finding the relevant pieces of code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:21
msgid ""
"`--trace-warnings` will make Node.js show a stack trace for this warning "
"and other warnings that are printed by Node.js."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:22
msgid ""
"`--trace-deprecation` does the same thing, but only for deprecation "
"warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:23
msgid ""
"`--pending-deprecation` will show more types of deprecation warnings. In "
"particular, it will show the `Buffer()` deprecation warning, even on "
"Node.js 8."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:25
msgid "You can set these flags using an environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:40
msgid "Finding problematic bits of code using linters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:42
msgid ""
"Eslint rules [no-buffer-constructor](https://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-"
"buffer-constructor) or [node/no-deprecated-"
"api](https://github.com/mysticatea/eslint-plugin-"
"node/blob/master/docs/rules/no-deprecated-api.md) also find calls to "
"deprecated `Buffer()` API. Those rules are included in some pre-sets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:47
msgid ""
"There is a drawback, though, that it doesn't always [work "
"correctly](https://github.com/chalker/safer-buffer#why-not-safe-buffer) "
"when `Buffer` is overriden e.g. with a polyfill, so recommended is a "
"combination of this and some other method described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:52
msgid "<a id=\"variant-1\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:53
msgid "Variant 1: Drop support for Node.js ≤ 4.4.x and 5.0.0 — 5.9.x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:55
msgid ""
"This is the recommended solution nowadays that would imply only minimal "
"overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:57
msgid ""
"The Node.js 5.x release line has been unsupported since July 2016, and "
"the Node.js 4.x release line reaches its End of Life in April 2018 (→ "
"[Schedule](https://github.com/nodejs/Release#release-schedule)). This "
"means that these versions of Node.js will *not* receive any updates, even"
" in case of security issues, so using these release lines should be "
"avoided, if at all possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:59
msgid ""
"What you would do in this case is to convert all `new Buffer()` or "
"`Buffer()` calls to use `Buffer.alloc()` or `Buffer.from()`, in the "
"following way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:61
msgid "For `new Buffer(number)`, replace it with `Buffer.alloc(number)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:62
msgid ""
"For `new Buffer(string)` (or `new Buffer(string, encoding)`), replace it "
"with `Buffer.from(string)` (or `Buffer.from(string, encoding)`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:63
msgid ""
"For all other combinations of arguments (these are much rarer), also "
"replace `new Buffer(...arguments)` with `Buffer.from(...arguments)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:65
msgid ""
"Note that `Buffer.alloc()` is also _faster_ on the current Node.js "
"versions than `new Buffer(size).fill(0)`, which is what you would "
"otherwise need to ensure zero-filling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:68
msgid ""
"Enabling eslint rule [no-buffer-"
"constructor](https://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-buffer-constructor) or "
"[node/no-deprecated-api](https://github.com/mysticatea/eslint-plugin-"
"node/blob/master/docs/rules/no-deprecated-api.md) is recommended to avoid"
" accidential unsafe Buffer API usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:73
msgid ""
"There is also a [JSCodeshift codemod](https://github.com/joyeecheung"
"/node-dep-codemod#dep005) for automatically migrating Buffer constructors"
" to `Buffer.alloc()` or `Buffer.from()`. Note that it currently only "
"works with cases where the arguments are literals or where the "
"constructor is invoked with two arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:78
msgid ""
"_If you currently support those older Node.js versions and dropping them "
"would be a semver-major change for you, or if you support older branches "
"of your packages, consider using [Variant 2](#variant-2) or [Variant "
"3](#variant-3) on older branches, so people using those older branches "
"will also receive the fix. That way, you will eradicate potential issues "
"caused by unguarded Buffer API usage and your users will not observe a "
"runtime deprecation warning when running your code on Node.js 10._"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:84
msgid "<a id=\"variant-2\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:85
msgid "Variant 2: Use a polyfill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:87
msgid ""
"Utilize [safer-buffer](https://www.npmjs.com/package/safer-buffer) as a "
"polyfill to support older Node.js versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:90
msgid ""
"You would take exacly the same steps as in [Variant 1](#variant-1), but "
"with a polyfill `const Buffer = require('safer-buffer').Buffer` in all "
"files where you use the new `Buffer` api."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:93
msgid ""
"Make sure that you do not use old `new Buffer` API — in any files where "
"the line above is added, using old `new Buffer()` API will _throw_. It "
"will be easy to notice that in CI, though."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:96
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you could use [buffer-from](https://www.npmjs.com/package"
"/buffer-from) and/or [buffer-alloc](https://www.npmjs.com/package/buffer-"
"alloc) [ponyfills](https://ponyfill.com/) — those are great, the only "
"downsides being 4 deps in the tree and slightly more code changes to "
"migrate off them (as you would be using e.g. `Buffer.from` under a "
"different name). If you need only `Buffer.from` polyfilled — `buffer-"
"from` alone which comes with no extra dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:102
msgid ""
"_Alternatively, you could use [safe-buffer](https://www.npmjs.com/package"
"/safe-buffer) — it also provides a polyfill, but takes a different "
"approach which has [it's drawbacks](https://github.com/chalker/safer-"
"buffer#why-not-safe-buffer). It will allow you to also use the older `new"
" Buffer()` API in your code, though — but that's arguably a benefit, as "
"it is problematic, can cause issues in your code, and will start emitting"
" runtime deprecation warnings starting with Node.js 10._"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:109
msgid ""
"Note that in either case, it is important that you also remove all calls "
"to the old Buffer API manually — just throwing in `safe-buffer` doesn't "
"fix the problem by itself, it just provides a polyfill for the new API. I"
" have seen people doing that mistake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:113
msgid ""
"Enabling eslint rule [no-buffer-"
"constructor](https://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-buffer-constructor) or "
"[node/no-deprecated-api](https://github.com/mysticatea/eslint-plugin-"
"node/blob/master/docs/rules/no-deprecated-api.md) is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:118
msgid ""
"_Don't forget to drop the polyfill usage once you drop support for "
"Node.js < 4.5.0._"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:120
msgid "<a id=\"variant-3\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:121
msgid "Variant 3 — manual detection, with safeguards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:123
msgid ""
"This is useful if you create Buffer instances in only a few places (e.g. "
"one), or you have your own wrapper around them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:126
msgid "Buffer(0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:128
msgid ""
"This special case for creating empty buffers can be safely replaced with "
"`Buffer.concat([])`, which returns the same result all the way down to "
"Node.js 0.8.x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:131
msgid "Buffer(notNumber)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:133
msgid "Before:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:139
msgid "After:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:152
msgid "`encoding` is optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:154
msgid ""
"Note that the `typeof notNumber` before `new Buffer` is required (for "
"cases when `notNumber` argument is not hard-coded) and _is not caused by "
"the deprecation of Buffer constructor_ — it's exactly _why_ the Buffer "
"constructor is deprecated. Ecosystem packages lacking this type-check "
"caused numereous security issues — situations when unsanitized user input"
" could end up in the `Buffer(arg)` create problems ranging from DoS to "
"leaking sensitive information to the attacker from the process memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:160
msgid ""
"When `notNumber` argument is hardcoded (e.g. literal `\"abc\"` or "
"`[0,1,2]`), the `typeof` check can be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:163
msgid ""
"Also note that using TypeScript does not fix this problem for you — when "
"libs written in `TypeScript` are used from JS, or when user input ends up"
" there — it behaves exactly as pure JS, as all type checks are "
"translation-time only and are not present in the actual JS code which TS "
"compiles to."
msgstr ""

