#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:209
msgid "<a id=\"design-flaws\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:210
msgid "What is wrong with the `Buffer` constructor?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:212
msgid ""
"The `Buffer` constructor could be used to create a buffer in many "
"different ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:214
msgid ""
"`new Buffer(42)` creates a `Buffer` of 42 bytes. Before Node.js 8, this "
"buffer contained *arbitrary memory* for performance reasons, which could "
"include anything ranging from program source code to passwords and "
"encryption keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:217
msgid ""
"`new Buffer('abc')` creates a `Buffer` that contains the UTF-8-encoded "
"version of the string `'abc'`. A second argument could specify another "
"encoding: For example, `new Buffer(string, 'base64')` could be used to "
"convert a Base64 string into the original sequence of bytes that it "
"represents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:221
msgid "There are several other combinations of arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:223
msgid ""
"This meant that, in code like `var buffer = new Buffer(foo);`, *it is not"
" possible to tell what exactly the contents of the generated buffer are* "
"without knowing the type of `foo`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:226
msgid ""
"Sometimes, the value of `foo` comes from an external source. For example,"
" this function could be exposed as a service on a web server, converting "
"a UTF-8 string into its Base64 form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:238
msgid "Note that this code does *not* validate the type of `req.body.string`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:240
msgid ""
"`req.body.string` is expected to be a string. If this is the case, all "
"goes well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:241
msgid "`req.body.string` is controlled by the client that sends the request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:242
msgid ""
"If `req.body.string` is the *number* `50`, the `rawBytes` would be 50 "
"bytes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:243
msgid "Before Node.js 8, the content would be uninitialized"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:244
msgid "After Node.js 8, the content would be `50` bytes with the value `0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:246
msgid ""
"Because of the missing type check, an attacker could intentionally send a"
" number as part of the request. Using this, they can either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:249
msgid ""
"Read uninitialized memory. This **will** leak passwords, encryption keys "
"and other kinds of sensitive information. (Information leak)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:251
msgid ""
"Force the program to allocate a large amount of memory. For example, when"
" specifying `500000000` as the input value, each request will allocate "
"500MB of memory. This can be used to either exhaust the memory available "
"of a program completely and make it crash, or slow it down significantly."
" (Denial of Service)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:256
msgid ""
"Both of these scenarios are considered serious security issues in a real-"
"world web server context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:259
msgid ""
"when using `Buffer.from(req.body.string)` instead, passing a number will "
"always throw an exception instead, giving a controlled behaviour that can"
" always be handled by the program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:263
msgid "<a id=\"ecosystem-usage\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:264
msgid ""
"The `Buffer()` constructor has been deprecated for a while. Is this "
"really an issue?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/safer-buffer_Porting-Buffer.md:266
msgid ""
"Surveys of code in the `npm` ecosystem have shown that the `Buffer()` "
"constructor is still widely used. This includes new code, and overall "
"usage of such code has actually been *increasing*."
msgstr ""

